WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
Most rule books have two columns.

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.480
Allowed, and forbidden.

3
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.330
Islamic law, as many
Muslims understand it,

4
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.990
has five verdicts for any action.

5
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.410
A scale that runs from must, to must not.

6
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.770
Near the bottom sits a strange one.

7
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.400
Disliked, but not forbidden.

8
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.830
Why would a religion need
a disliked category at all?

9
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.420
In this mission, you'll
build the whole scale,

10
00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.730
with examples for each of the five.

11
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.240
Then you'll see how different schools
place the same act in different places.

12
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:36.130
Your mission: explain why Islamic
law needs a disliked category at all.
